In our evaluation, we used a 5-shot in-context learning (ICL) paradigm to assess the model’s ability to adapt to new tasks from a limited number of examples. This approach is predicated on providing the model with five illustrative input-output pairs (the support set) within the prompt itself, followed by the actual query for which a prediction is sought. The model is then expected to generalize from these examples to generate the correct output for the unseen query.
